Ninjavenge
==========

A lane-defense action game. You are Ren, the last ninja of the Otaku clan.
Cowboys, robots and jack-o-lanterns raided your home and now travel its roads.
Stop them: every enemy that slips past costs you a heart.

Original version: 4/27/2016, Mark D Hangarter.
Version 2 (2026): rewrite with wave-based play, enemy attacks, combos, a boss,
and a restructured codebase. The PDF in "Game Manual" describes version 1.


Running
-------
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    cd src
    python main.py


Controls
--------
    Left / Right      run
    Up / Down         hop to the next lane (attack/throw mid-air for a jump attack)
    A  (or J / Z)     katana - hits everything in reach, sends bullets back at the shooter
    S  (or K / X)     throw kunai (short cooldown)
    Esc / P / F1      pause
Menus work with the arrow keys + Enter, or the mouse.


Enemies
-------
    Cowboy       fast, fragile; flashes "!" then shoots down his lane
    Robot        armored; a kunai staggers it, slashes do double damage while staggered
    Jack         revives after death unless you SLASH the pumpkin before the ring closes
                 (kunai pass straight through it)
    Bosses       every 5th wave, alternating Sir Clank (knight) and Rex (dino).
                 A kunai during their "!" wind-up interrupts the attack.
                 A boss that gets through costs 3 hearts.

Chain kills without losing a heart to raise the score multiplier (up to x5).
Air kills, deflected bullets and smashed pumpkins earn bonus points.
Deflected bullets hit enemies like a kunai: cowboys and jacks take damage, armored
foes are staggered, and a ricochet can interrupt a boss wind-up.
High scores are saved to ~/.ninjavenge/scores.json.


Ryo and the Dojo Shop
---------------------
Kills earn ryo (cowboy 1, jack 2, robot 3, boss 25) and clearing wave N pays 2*N.
Ryo is banked when a run ends and spent in the Dojo Shop (main menu or game over):
    Swift Kunai       kunai fly 20% faster per level (3 levels)
    Quick Hands       kunai cooldown 20% shorter per level (3 levels)
    Sharpened Katana  +0.5 katana damage per level (3 levels)
    Extra Heart       +1 max heart per level (2 levels)
    Shinobi Mode      teleport between lanes instead of jumping (toggle on/off in the shop)
Progress is saved to ~/.ninjavenge/profile.json. Prices and rates live in
ninjavenge/upgrades.py and ninjavenge/config.py.


Code layout (src/)
------------------
    main.py                 entry point
    ninjavenge/config.py    every tunable number (speeds, timings, lanes, scoring)
    ninjavenge/app.py       the single game loop + scene stack
    ninjavenge/assets.py    cached image/animation/sound loading (frames pre-flipped)
    ninjavenge/animation.py time-based animation
    ninjavenge/world.py     in-play state and the rules connecting entities
    ninjavenge/waves.py     wave definitions + WaveDirector (pure logic)
    ninjavenge/scoring.py   score and combo multiplier (pure logic)
    ninjavenge/highscore.py persistent high-score table
    ninjavenge/upgrades.py  shop upgrades, Loadout, ryo earnings (pure logic)
    ninjavenge/profile.py   saved ryo balance and purchased upgrades
    ninjavenge/entities/    Ninja, enemies, projectiles, particles
    ninjavenge/scenes/      menu, game, tutorial, pause, game over, info screens
    ninjavenge/ui.py        menus, background, HUD
    tests/                  unit + headless integration tests


Boss art
--------
The boss sprites are pzUH's CC0 GameArt2D packs (see CREDITS). To regenerate the
game-sized frames from the original zips:
    python tools/prepare_boss_art.py <FreeKnight/png> <FreeDinoSprite/png>


Tests
-----
    cd src
    python -m unittest discover tests
